From 078531d08bbdbab5f1a8dea1d1f46eb4821c2998 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <zenithblue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:50:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 85/89] jm-v7 112: release the gs_bo_pool free list on pool
 reset and trim

Rationale: csf-v11 220 frees the command pool's BO free lists on
vkResetCommandPool(RELEASE_RESOURCES) and vkTrimCommandPool; the v6/v7
geometry emulation pool (gs_bo_pool, jm-v7 030) is added by this series,
so its free list is released here (perf review 2026-10-22 K6: "gs slabs
stay at their GPU-faulted committed size").
Expected gain: memory on v6/v7 after GS/tess/xfb-heavy command buffers:
the grown gs slabs (up to the faulted commit each) are freed on
reset-with-release or trim instead of staying committed until the pool
is destroyed.

Knob: PANVK_CMD_POOL_TRIM=0 (csf-v11 220) restores the old behaviour.
Arch: gs_pool is used by v6/v7 only. Not device-tested.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_cmd_pool.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_cmd_pool.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_cmd_pool.c
index d91fcec6..ab97174d 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_cmd_pool.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_cmd_pool.c
@@ -99,6 +99,8 @@ panvk_cmd_pool_release_free_bos(struct panvk_cmd_pool *pool)
 {
    panvk_bo_pool_cleanup(&pool->cs_bo_pool);
    panvk_bo_pool_cleanup(&pool->desc_bo_pool);
+   /* jm-v7 112: the v6/v7 geometry emulation slabs (jm-v7 030). */
+   panvk_bo_pool_cleanup(&pool->gs_bo_pool);
    panvk_bo_pool_cleanup(&pool->varying_bo_pool);
    panvk_bo_pool_cleanup(&pool->tls_bo_pool);
    panvk_bo_pool_cleanup(&pool->tls_big_bo_pool);
-- 
